+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; Free-Text Veterinarian Search Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, on the reason that owner search demonstrates paged prefix search once. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was deliberately declined stayed unknown.
+
+On 2026-08-17 the owner asked for the veterinarian list to be filterable by specialty. Read against NG-9 as written, that request looked declined: a specialty filter is a way of searching veterinarians. The owner decided the row rather than letting the request reopen it by implication.
+
+The same request reinstated the machine-readable veterinarian list as a supported surface. `REQ-VET-002`, withdrawn 2026-07-31 as an implementation artifact, stays withdrawn and its ID is not reused.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter. Rejected by the owner: the directory already shows each veterinarian's specialties, so selecting on one adds no new information to the page.
+2. **Drop NG-9.** Open veterinarian search generally. Rejected: free-text search over veterinarians would repeat the owner-search pattern, which is the reason the row exists.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search stays out; filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows comes in.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed, not withdrawn. Free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian remains out of scope. Filtering the veterinarian directory by a specialty it already displays is in scope, and is recorded as `REQ-VET-003`.
+
+The filter is a URL contract in this requirement. Neither published form gains a form, dropdown, or other page control; a visible control may come as a follow-up request.
+
+A future request touching NG-9 beyond this narrowing proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row. Its table entry names both halves.
+- The machine-readable veterinarian list becomes a supported surface with a requirement behind it, so it is no longer a route pending removal.
+- Filtering by an attribute already on the page is now the recorded boundary for the directory. Free-text search over any non-owner entity still needs its own owner decision.
+- Whether a padded specialty name is trimmed is left open, recorded in the PRD's Open Questions.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [`REQ-VET-003`](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing lets in.
