 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The same directory is published a second way, in a machine-readable form for callers that consume the list rather than read it. Both forms answer a request naming one specialty by listing only the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. The named specialty must match a held specialty in full, disregarding letter case; the start of a name is not enough. The name is supplied with the request itself, and neither form gains a form, dropdown, or other page control here. Paging still applies to the filtered page, and its links carry the named specialty so a filtered list stays navigable.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable form is requested, then it carries every veterinarian with their specialties.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a request naming a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the directory page is opened, then only those veterinarians are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given that same request, when the machine-readable form is requested, then it carries only those veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty differing from a held one only by letter case, when either form is requested, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty that is only the start of a held one, when either form is requested, then it matches no veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty no veterinarian holds, when either form is requested, then it is returned as usual, carrying no veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or blank specialty name, when either form is requested, then every veterinarian is listed, as if none had been named.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty named at all, when either form is requested, then it behaves as it did before this requirement.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered page carrying more veterinarians than fit, when a paging link is followed, then the next page is filtered by the same specialty.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A named specialty matching no veterinarian is not an error; the page and the machine-readable form are returned as usual, empty of veterinarians.
+3. A specialty name padded with spaces matches nothing, because the match is on the whole name. Only an empty or all-space name counts as none named. See [Open Questions](#open-questions).
 
